{"t": 1792002235.754, "event": "person", "step": "L5", "command": {"do": "home", "who": "bo", "url": "http://svrngs.localhost:62373/", "words": ["Open Sam’s events", "did not answer"], "shot": "21-bo-L5"}, "status": 200, "refused": null, "url": "http://svrngs.localhost:62373/", "text": "Your groups\n\nThis page is yours, on this computer alone. On it you see your groups and who is in each, open what the people in them lend you, each in a tab of its own beside this page, open a link to it someone sent in your group’s chat, open each group’s folder, make a group, make a link to invite someone or to add your phone or another computer, and choose how many people at once may use what this computer lends them.\n\nA link works for a day, while this computer is on. Making one stops the last link you made letting anyone new in; everyone it let in stays.\n\nA program on this computer, such as one you chat with a friend’s model in, reaches what is lent to you at the address beside it: its Copy button copies it, for you to paste where the program asks for an address.\n\nThe House\n\nPeople: Sam, Cy, Bo\n\nThe House’s folder is on this computer at /tmp/doclink-run/bo/svrngs/The House\n\nOpen this folder\n\nMake a link to invite someone to The HouseMake a link to add your phone or another computer of yours\n\nSam's computer did not answer, so what they lend is not listed.\nOpen a link from your group\n\nThe link: Open it\n\nMake a group\n\nA name for the group: Your name in it: Make a group\n\nWhat this computer lends\n\nThis computer lends nothing.\n\nYour home page, the same address each time svrngs starts: http://svrngs.localhost:62373/\n\nDone in a terminal\n\nA few things are not done on this page yet. For each, open the Terminal app and type its line, with your own words in place of each <…>:\n\nLend your groups a program this computer runs, such as a model: svrngs share <the number after the colon in its address>, as in svrngs share 8080 for one at http://localhost:8080. svrngs then says what it lent, and to whom.\nRemove someone from a group: svrngs remove <their name> --group <the group’s name>\n\nLeaving a group is not possible yet: nothing in svrngs does it.", "title": "Your groups", "sections": [], "buttons": ["Open this folder", "Make a link to invite someone to The House", "Make a link to add your phone or another computer of yours", "Open it", "Make a group"], "ms": 3210, "met": true}
